course: dictionary
lesson: 3453
title: Fade: losing colour, light and sound
level: primary-5
stars: 2
explain: «Dyes can also leave: they wash out, rub off and fade in sunlight.» Here fade means losing colour slowly. The sunlight is the clue: over time, the sun makes colours go pale.
explain: «The music faded» and «the light faded» do not mention colour at all. Something is getting quieter or dimmer until you can no longer notice it. Ask yourself: is something losing colour, or is it getting weaker until it disappears?
explain: A sound can fade too. «The quack fades away softly» means the sound gets quieter as it goes, until it is hard to hear. Fade is one word with several meanings, so read the words around it to choose the right one.
fact: Fade is a verb: fade, fades, faded, fading.
fact: To fade can mean to slowly lose colour or brightness, as in «fade in sunlight».
fact: To fade can also mean to slowly become quieter, weaker or less clear until it disappears, as in «the light fades like evening».
fact: When flowers fade, they wilt and die.
fact: Fade is also a noun, «a fade», used in film and music for a slow change in brightness or loudness.
exercise: «Dyes can also leave: they wash out, rub off and fade in sunlight.» What does fade mean here? | To shout loudly | *To slowly lose colour | To grow taller | To freeze solid
exercise: «Dive down and the light fades like evening.» What is happening to the light? | It turns into a colour | It gets brighter and brighter | It starts to rain | *It gets dimmer until it is gone
exercise: Jo's rose has faded. What has happened to it? | *It has wilted and died | It has been put in a vase of water | It has grown a metre taller | It has been painted red
test: «The music faded until we could hardly hear it.» What does faded mean here? | *It got quieter and weaker until it disappeared | It got louder and louder | It stopped with a loud bang | It changed to a different song
test: «Faded jeans» are jeans that have | Been made from thick wool | *Lost their colour and gone pale | Grown longer in the wash | Been sewn with gold thread
exam: Mia says fade only means a colour going pale. Is she right? | Yes, that is the only meaning | *No, it can also mean a sound or light getting weaker until it disappears | Yes, and it only happens in sunlight | No, it means to jump up high
